sec.p:
Consider now the as the ground truth the line y = x, and sample the set T including twenty positive integer points T = {ti = (xi,yTi) = (i,i) 1 ≤ i ≤ 20} on the line. Define REAL = {ri = (xi,yRi) = (i,i + N(i)) 1 ≤ i ≤ 20} as the same points of T with a small amount of noise N(i) on the y axes, so that ri are close but not lying on the y = x straight line. Consider now two predicting regression models:
The set PREDc = T representing the correct model;
The set PREDw representing the (wrong) model with points defined as pwi = f(xi), for f the 10-th degree polynomial exactly passing through the points ri for 1 ≤ i ≤ 10.
